title: "MATLAB Implementation and Input Data for the Comparative Assessment of ELCC, ECP, and Firm Capacity Methodologies (IEEE ETCM 2026, Paper ID 119)"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-07"
license: MIT
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  DOI: replace DOI_PLACEHOLDER with the Zenodo DOI after
#  creating the release (e.g. 10.5281/zenodo.1234567)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
doi: "DOI_PLACEHOLDER"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiegoAriasCazco/ETCM_2026_PaperID119_ELCCandECP"
url: "https://github.com/DiegoAriasCazco/ETCM_2026_PaperID119_ELCCandECP"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB implementation and input datasets supporting the paper
  "Comparative Assessment of ELCC, ECP, and Firm Capacity
  Methodologies for Resource Adequacy in Renewable-Dominated
  Power Systems", presented at the 2026 IEEE Eighth Ecuador
  Technical Chapters Meeting (ETCM 2026). Contains a unified
  probabilistic-deterministic framework based on exact recursive
  COPT convolution and 8760-hour chronological LOLE evaluation,
  applied to the Ecuador National Interconnected System (SNI)
  2025 with real NSRDB solar profiles.

